		<content type="html" xml:base="http://localhost/opengd77/viewtopic.php?t=3695&amp;p=28731#p28731"><![CDATA[
The tab character is used to force a spreadsheet program to treat the value as text and not a number.  It was intended to prevent channel names (which can contain numbers but are really text) being interpreted as numbers and loosing digits. It is not really needed on frequencies . If a tab is present it should be ignored on import. So it should be optional. At least that is the way it is supposed to work. If anything I would have expected the quotes to be more of a problem. <br><br>I will have to check the latest CPS to make sure it still works as intended. <br><br>In the mean time if you want to confirm that the tabs are the problem it is easy enough to edit the line in question using a text editor such as notepad. CSV files are just text files after all.<br><br>Colin G4EML.<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="http://localhost/opengd77/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=87">G4EML</a> — Tue Jan 16, 2024 10:54 pm</p><hr />
]]></content>
